.DS_Store
__MACOSX/
._*

# Destination-project generated learning/prototype output may be ignored locally if desired.
# prototypes/
# learning/

# Local planning only — not pushed
.features/

# This repository's own Work Tracking config. Local like `.features/`, and for
# the same reason: `context` is a directory entry in the copy list, so a
# committed copy would ship Pathfinder's tracker configuration to every
# destination project and defeat the off switch — which is the absence of this
# very file — on first install. Anchored so only the root one is ignored.
# Not the enforcement: `neverShips()` in the installer and the staging script
# is. This keeps it out of version control; that keeps it out of the tarball.
/context/tracker.md

# This repository's own transient session state, ignored for the same reason
# and by the same pair of mechanisms. `/feature load` and `handoff` write these
# on first use; neither is durable project truth, and a committed copy would
# be one maintainer's in-flight work showing up in everybody's diff. Durable
# context — project-overview.md, features/, history.md — is tracked normally.
/context/current-feature.md
/context/handoff.md

# Generated harness adapters. Pathfinder commits adapters only for the harness
# its own maintainers use — `.claude/skills/` is tracked and CI checks it is
# fresh. Every other harness is generated on demand, so its output is ignored
# here rather than becoming a second tracked directory. `.agents/skills/` is
# the Codex destination, which a maintainer running the installer against this
# repository can materialize locally.
/.agents/skills/

# Per-machine Claude Code settings. Records one developer's tool permissions and
# has no meaning in another checkout. Ignored by path, not by directory, because
# `.claude/skills/` above it must stay tracked — ignoring `/.claude/` would take
# the adapters with it.
/.claude/settings.local.json

# Docs site. Dependencies and build output only — `site/package-lock.json` is
# committed so the pinned toolchain is reproducible. The brand files under
# `site/public/` are copies made by `site/scripts/sync-brand.mjs` from the
# single originals in `assets/`, so they are ignored one path at a time — the
# directory itself holds hand-written files, such as the web app manifest, that
# must stay tracked.
/site/node_modules/
/site/dist/
/site/.astro/
/site/public/favicon.svg
/site/public/favicon-32.png
/site/public/icon-192.png
/site/public/icon-512.png
/site/public/icon-maskable-512.png
/site/public/apple-touch-icon-180.png

# Transient. `npm pack` stages the kit into the installer package so npm can
# see it — `files` cannot reach outside the package directory — and unstages it
# afterwards. The copy at the repository root stays the only one in version
# control. Paths are anchored so the root context/, skills/, etc. are unaffected.
/packages/create-pathfinder/AGENTS.md
/packages/create-pathfinder/CLAUDE.md
/packages/create-pathfinder/LICENSE
/packages/create-pathfinder/context/
/packages/create-pathfinder/roles/
/packages/create-pathfinder/skills/
/packages/create-pathfinder/templates/
/packages/create-pathfinder/*.tgz
